## 2. Lease in Postgres
   concept: each replica runs one statement every second: take the scheduler row if it is expired, or extend it if it is already mine; expires_at comes from the database's now(), never a local clock; only the holder runs the job
   06:26:23 [c] started (pid 58995), lease TTL 3s, renew every 1s
   06:26:23 [a] started (pid 58993), lease TTL 3s, renew every 1s
   06:26:23 [b] started (pid 58994), lease TTL 3s, renew every 1s
   06:26:23 [c] acquired the lease, term 1
   06:26:23 [a] follower, c leads (term 1)
   06:26:23 [c] job ran, term 1
   06:26:23 [b] follower, c leads (term 1)
   06:26:24 [c] job ran, term 1
   06:26:25 [c] job ran, term 1
   06:26:26 [c] job ran, term 1
